<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p><em>Effective date: August 8, 2026</em></p>

<p>
Tlociu ("we", "us") is a personal movie-watchlist application operated by
Kevin Goess. This policy describes what information the application collects,
how it is used, and the choices you have. Questions can be sent to
<a href="mailto:kevin@goess.org">kevin@goess.org</a>.
</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>

<h3>Information from Google Sign-In</h3>
<p>
Tlociu uses "Sign in with Google" as its only login method. When you sign in,
Google sends us an identity token containing your basic profile information:
your email address, your name, and the URL of your profile picture. We use
only your <strong>email address</strong>, to match you to an existing Tlociu
account. We do not store your name or profile picture, and we do not request
access to any other Google data (no Gmail, Drive, Calendar, or Contacts
access).
</p>

<h3>Account information</h3>
<p>
Your account record consists of a username, your email address, and the date
the account was created. Accounts are created manually by the operator;
signing in with Google does not create an account.
</p>

<h3>Content you create</h3>
<p>
The watchlist entries you create — movie titles, notes, and dates — are
stored in our database and are associated with your account. They are visible
only to you when signed in, unless you explicitly mark an entry as public.
</p>

<h3>Cookies</h3>
<p>
We use cookies only to keep you signed in. After a successful Google sign-in
we set two cookies (your Google identity token and the login method), which
expire after 72 hours. We do not use analytics, advertising, or tracking
cookies.
</p>

<h2>How we use your information</h2>
<p>We use the information above solely to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>authenticate you when you sign in;</li>
    <li>show you your own watchlist and let you manage it.</li>
</ul>
<p>
We do not sell your information, use it for advertising, or share it with
third parties, with one narrow exception: movie-title searches you type are
sent to The Movie Database (TMDB) to look up film details. Those queries are
not accompanied by your name, email address, or any other identifying
information.
</p>

<h2>Google user data and Limited Use</h2>
<p>
Tlociu's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to
the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google
API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
</p>

<h2>Data storage and security</h2>
<p>
Your data is stored in a database on our server, accessible only to the
operator. Connections to the application are encrypted with HTTPS.
</p>

<h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
<p>
We keep your account information and watchlist entries for as long as your
account is active. To have your account and all associated data deleted,
email <a href="mailto:kevin@goess.org">kevin@goess.org</a>. You can also
revoke Tlociu's access to your Google account at any time at
<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>
Tlociu is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
information from them.
</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this address with
an updated effective date.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
Kevin Goess — <a href="mailto:kevin@goess.org">kevin@goess.org</a>
</p>
